# MintPlaza environment configuration
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit .env.local.

# --- Supabase (added in build step 2) ---
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://bfmjslvpssufcujfhbce.supabase.co
# Settings -> API -> Project API keys -> anon / public.
# Publishable by design: row-level security protects the data, not this key.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Server-only, and a real secret — it bypasses row-level security entirely.
# Never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_, never commit it, never paste it in chat.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Demo content ---
# When "on", the interface renders clearly-badged example content so the
# design can be reviewed before real data exists. The site is published now, so
# this is off: a visitor who spots one fake listing concludes the whole thing is
# fake, and there is no recovering that first impression. See src/lib/demo.ts.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_MODE=off

# --- Roblox sign-in ---
# There is nothing to put here. Roblox's client ID and secret are configured in
# the Supabase dashboard as a custom OIDC provider named exactly
# "custom:roblox", and Supabase does the token exchange itself — so this
# application never holds the secret and cannot leak it.
# Setup steps: docs/roblox-sign-in.md

# --- Development sign-in ---
# Two ordinary accounts for testing the signed-in half of the site without
# going out to Roblox each time. Needs a non-production build as well, so
# shipping the flag by accident still does not open a password login.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_LOGIN=on
# NO NEXT_PUBLIC_ PREFIX, and that is the whole point. A NEXT_PUBLIC_ value is
# substituted into the JavaScript at build time and ships to every visitor —
# this one was, and the dev accounts were takeable by anyone who read the
# bundle. Read only by the server action in src/lib/actions/dev-login.ts.
DEV_PASSWORD=

# --- Level Up: where the buy button goes ---
# The hosted checkout page for each price point. Nothing in this codebase can
# take a card and nothing should — handling card data means PCI scope, which is
# not somewhere a site run by one person belongs. These are links to a payment
# provider's own page.
#
# Leave them empty and the upgrade screen says honestly that Level Up is not on
# sale yet. That is the correct behaviour, not a placeholder: a button that
# pretends to take money and does not is worse than no button.
LEVEL_UP_CHECKOUT_URL_INR=
LEVEL_UP_CHECKOUT_URL_USD=

# --- Level Up: the payment webhook ---
# Shared secret between this site and whatever takes the money. The paying side
# signs each delivery with it; /api/level-up/webhook checks the signature and
# refuses anything else.
#
# NO NEXT_PUBLIC_ PREFIX. A NEXT_PUBLIC_ value is substituted into the
# JavaScript at build time and ships to every visitor, and this one grants a
# paid feature to anybody holding it. The proof script fails the build if it is
# ever prefixed.
#
# With this unset the webhook refuses EVERYTHING with a 503, including a
# perfectly signed request — it fails closed. Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('node:crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
LEVEL_UP_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- Referral partners (optional) ---
# Our id with each value site, attached to outbound links once an agreement
# exists. One per partner key from src/lib/referrals.ts, upper-cased with
# hyphens as underscores. Server-only, so rotating one is a deploy rather than
# a rebuild. Nothing breaks when they are absent: the links still work, and the
# "we earn commission" disclosure correctly stays hidden.
# PARTNER_ID_COSMIC_VALUES=
# PARTNER_ID_ELVEBREDD=
# PARTNER_ID_BLOX_FRUITS_VALUES=
# PARTNER_ID_GAG2GG=
# PARTNER_ID_GAME_GUIDE=

# --- Where the site lives ---
# Only needed once a real domain is bought — set it to the full origin, e.g.
# https://mintplaza.com. Until then Vercel's own production URL is used
# automatically, so this can stay empty.
#
# What it controls: the absolute URL of the icon and the link-preview image.
# With no origin to resolve against, Next falls back to http://localhost:3000
# and every link shared in Discord or a video description shows a broken
# preview. See src/lib/site.ts.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The rewarded ad in front of finalising a deal
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Leave these unset and there is no ad step: the finalise button finalises.
# That is the state the site ships in, and it is a working state, not a
# placeholder.
#
# BEFORE SETTING THESE, know that requiring somebody to watch an ad to unlock
# a feature is "incentivised" traffic. With ordinary AdSense display units that
# breaks Google's programme policies and is one of the faster ways to lose an
# AdSense account. Rewarded ads are a different, permitted format, and AdSense
# does not offer them for a general website — they come from AdMob (apps),
# Google Ad Manager, or a gaming ad network. Point this at one of those, never
# at a plain AdSense display slot.
#
# The provider's script must expose one function on window:
#
#   window.mintplazaRewardedAd = (unit) => Promise<boolean>   // true = reward earned
#
# Whatever happens, the deal still finalises — see src/lib/ads.ts for why.
NEXT_PUBLIC_REWARDED_AD_PROVIDER=
NEXT_PUBLIC_REWARDED_AD_SRC=
NEXT_PUBLIC_REWARDED_AD_UNIT=
